{"bendscript":"0.1","blocks":[{"id":"blk-58093","kind":"heading","level":1,"spans":[{"id":"spn-67383","text":"TickTickClock Documentation"}]},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-58095","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67384","marks":["bold"],"text":"Every tick is a learning opportunity. Every pattern has a rhythm. Temporal intelligence that never forgets."}]}],"id":"blk-58094","kind":"quote"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-58097","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67385","marks":["bold"],"text":"Part of the [&] Protocol stack"},{"id":"spn-67386","text":" · "},{"id":"spn-67387","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/ECOSYSTEM.md"}],"text":"Ecosystem overview"},{"id":"spn-67388","text":" · "},{"id":"spn-67389","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/PULSE/docs/THREE_PROTOCOL_STACK.md"}],"text":"Three-protocol stack"},{"id":"spn-67390","text":" · "},{"id":"spn-67391","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/STACK_COMPLETION.md"}],"text":"Stack status"}]}],"id":"blk-58096","kind":"quote"},{"id":"blk-58098","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67392","text":"Welcome to the documentation hub for "},{"id":"spn-67393","marks":["bold"],"text":"TickTickClock"},{"id":"spn-67394","text":" — the temporal intelligence layer for the [&] Protocol ecosystem. TickTickClock provides time-series anomaly detection, forecasting, and pattern recognition as continual learning services."}]},{"id":"blk-58099","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67395","text":"TickTickClock is the "},{"id":"spn-67396","marks":["code"],"text":"&time"},{"id":"spn-67397","text":" primitive provider, exposing "},{"id":"spn-67398","marks":["code"],"text":"&time.anomaly"},{"id":"spn-67399","text":", "},{"id":"spn-67400","marks":["code"],"text":"&time.forecast"},{"id":"spn-67401","text":", and "},{"id":"spn-67402","marks":["code"],"text":"&time.pattern"},{"id":"spn-67403","text":" capability contracts. It does not store business data, host agents, or manage workflows — it ingests temporal signals, learns their structure continuously, and returns intelligence to upstream consumers."}]},{"id":"blk-58100","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67404","text":"---"}]},{"id":"blk-58101","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-67405","text":"The Problem"}]},{"id":"blk-58102","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67406","text":"Time-series intelligence in production systems is fragmented. Anomaly detection runs as a batch job. Forecasting lives in a notebook. Pattern detection is a dashboard someone checks on Mondays. None of these systems learn continuously, and none of them talk to each other."}]},{"id":"blk-58103","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67407","text":"Meanwhile, underlying models suffer from catastrophic forgetting — retrained monthly on a window of recent data, discarding everything about long-range seasonality. Multi-timescale temporal behavior requires multi-timescale memory, and no production system provides it."}]},{"id":"blk-58104","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67408","text":"TickTickClock solves this with:"}]},{"id":"blk-58105","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-58107","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67409","marks":["bold"],"text":"Continual learning"},{"id":"spn-67410","text":" — models update at inference time, no batch retraining"}]}],"id":"blk-58106","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-58109","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67411","marks":["bold"],"text":"Multi-timescale memory"},{"id":"spn-67412","text":" — fast (seconds), medium (hours), slow (days), glacial (months)"}]}],"id":"blk-58108","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-58111","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67413","marks":["bold"],"text":"Streaming-first"},{"id":"spn-67414","text":" — designed for unbounded streams, not fixed datasets"}]}],"id":"blk-58110","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-58113","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67415","marks":["bold"],"text":"Edge-capable"},{"id":"spn-67416","text":" — SQLite + Bumblebee on constrained devices"}]}],"id":"blk-58112","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-58114","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67417","text":"---"}]},{"id":"blk-58115","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-67418","text":"Documentation Map"}]},{"id":"blk-58116","kind":"code","language":"text","text":":maxdepth: 1\n:caption: Homepages\n\n[&] Ampersand Box <https://ampersandboxdesign.com>\nGraphonomous <https://graphonomous.com>\nBendScript <https://bendscript.com>\nWebHost.Systems <https://webhost.systems>\nAgentelic <https://agentelic.com>\nAgenTroMatic <https://agentromatic.com>\nDelegatic <https://delegatic.com>\nDeliberatic <https://deliberatic.com>\nFleetPrompt <https://fleetprompt.com>\nGeoFleetic <https://geofleetic.com>\nOpenSentience <https://opensentience.org>\nSpecPrompt <https://specprompt.com>\nTickTickClock <https://ticktickclock.com>"},{"id":"blk-58117","kind":"code","language":"text","text":":maxdepth: 1\n:caption: Root Docs\n\n[&] Protocol Docs <https://docs.ampersandboxdesign.com>\nGraphonomous Docs <https://docs.graphonomous.com>\nBendScript Docs <https://docs.bendscript.com>\nWebHost.Systems Docs <https://docs.webhost.systems>\nAgentelic Docs <https://docs.agentelic.com>\nAgenTroMatic Docs <https://docs.agentromatic.com>\nDelegatic Docs <https://docs.delegatic.com>\nDeliberatic Docs <https://docs.deliberatic.com>\nFleetPrompt Docs <https://docs.fleetprompt.com>\nGeoFleetic Docs <https://docs.geofleetic.com>\nOpenSentience Docs <https://docs.opensentience.org>\nSpecPrompt Docs <https://docs.specprompt.com>\nTickTickClock Docs <https://docs.ticktickclock.com>"},{"id":"blk-58118","kind":"code","language":"text","text":":maxdepth: 2\n:caption: TickTickClock Docs\n\nspec/README"},{"id":"blk-58119","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-67419","text":"---"}]},{"id":"blk-58120","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-67420","text":"[&] Capability Contracts"}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-58122","sp